.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_REMOVE 3 2026-09-28 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_remove \- stage a delete marker for a named base member
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_remove("
.BI "        mpq_patch_s *" "patch,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stages a delete marker for an existing named member. Applying the published
patch hides that member from the base archive, but neither this call nor patch
publication modifies the base archive itself. A missing member cannot be
removed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
A NULL handle or missing member returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Malformed
identity, allocation, and write errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_begin (3),
